// vspace.rule -- SYNTHETIC (NO vendor data). Exercises voltage-aware /
// net-voltage-dependent spacing (fork feature #12): the spacing REQUIRED between
// two DIFFERENT nets grows with the voltage difference across the gap.
//
// Layer numbers are synthetic placeholders:
//   poly 2/0  cont 3/0  met1 4/0   |   vdd18 20/0  vdd50 21/0 (voltage markers)
//
//   VOLTAGE <marker> <volts>   a net that TOUCHES a shape on <marker> is held at
//                              <volts>. Unmarked nets are treated as 0 V.
//   VSPACE <layer> < <base> PER_VOLT <k>
//                              required(i,j) = base + k*|V_i - V_j|   [um]
//                              violation when the measured spacing is BELOW it.
//
// V.SP.M1 : base 0.20 um + 0.05 um per volt of difference.
//             1.8 V vs 1.8 V -> 0.20 + 0.05*0.0 = 0.20 um
//             1.8 V vs 5.0 V -> 0.20 + 0.05*3.2 = 0.36 um
//           so the SAME 0.30 um gap is legal inside one domain and illegal
//           across the two -- the check cannot be reproduced by any single
//           fixed-distance EXTERNAL rule.
//
// V.SP.M1.K0 : the identical rule with PER_VOLT 0 -> every required spacing
//           collapses to the 0.20 um base and the layout is clean. This is the
//           control: it proves the failure above comes from the VOLTAGE term.
//
// V.SP.NOK : no PER_VOLT modifier -> honest SKIP (a voltage-aware rule with no
//           voltage term is just EXTERNAL and must not masquerade as one).

LAYER poly   2 0
LAYER cont   3 0
LAYER met1   4 0
LAYER vdd18 20 0
LAYER vdd50 21 0

CONNECT poly met1 BY cont

VOLTAGE vdd18 1.8
VOLTAGE vdd50 5.0

V.SP.M1 {
  VSPACE met1 < 0.20 PER_VOLT 0.05
}

V.SP.M1.K0 {
  VSPACE met1 < 0.20 PER_VOLT 0
}

V.SP.NOK {
  VSPACE met1 < 0.20
}
